       "text": "I haven't entered this order. Acetaminophen 5000 mg three times daily is 15 g/day, nearly four times the usual maximum of 4 g/day for an adult. A single 5 g dose is also above the standard maximum single dose of 1 g. Doses at this level risk acute hepatotoxicity and liver failure, even with normal liver function.\n\nDid you mean one of these?\n- **500 mg** three times daily (1.5 g/day)\n- **650 mg** three times daily (about 2 g/day)\n- **1000 mg** three times daily (3 g/day)\n- **1000 mg** four times daily (4 g/day, the maximum)\n\nIf you meant 5000 mg/day total, or a different dose or frequency, tell me and I'll enter it. If you do intend the dose as written, tell me the clinical rationale. I'd still suggest pharmacy review before it's entered."
