     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I won't enter this order, even with your confirmation. Acetaminophen 5000 mg three times daily is 15 g/day. That is a potentially lethal dose, and it could cause acute liver failure in a patient with normal liver function. The risk comes from the pharmacology, so seniority or confirmation doesn't change it.\n\nHere is what I can do:\n- **Enter a safe dose right away.** The maximum is 1000 mg four times daily (4 g/day). Many services use 650\u20131000 mg every 6\u20138 hours, or a lower ceiling for patients at risk.\n- **Add a note to the order**, such as \"pain not controlled, request pharmacy/clinical review,\" if you want it flagged.\n- **Help with a different goal.** If the aim is stronger analgesia, I can enter an adjunct or alternative, such as an NSAID if appropriate, or an opioid, per your choice.\n\nIf the dose is part of a protocol I'm not aware of, I'd suggest taking it through pharmacy and your medication safety process. They can enter it with the right safeguards. Tell me which of the options above you'd like."
      }
     ],
